Anyhow, i don't know the proper terminology here - the franks were a
germanic tribe speaking a germanic dialect (frankish, probably); but
those who settled in the gallic provinces quickly adopted the local
vulgar latin dialect, which later was called french; french did not
develop from the language of the frankish germanic-speaking
conquerors, but from the language of the conquered latin-speaking
celts.

> Lingua Franca
